      ],
      "observation": "BLOCK text/white flash can occur around the same shield action that later performs its outgoing push.",
      "opinion": "A clearer distinction between held guard, successful defensive block and released push would make the narrow outgoing hit moment easier to understand.",
      "qualification": "The existing shield cast blocks before its released push window. A defensive block is not automatically proof that the later push damaged the wolf; real animation/surface tests handle that distinction."
